  "notes": "FIRST PASS, LARGELY UNVERIFIED. Read off 42px sprites by eye at 22x. Reviewed afterwards against the artwork and found substantially wrong: the far arm was drawn straight down the middle of the chest where no arm is painted, a far toe landed in empty background, knees sat at mid-thigh and the hip sat at the waist. Only head_top, paw_l (the cannon muzzle) and the two toes follow readable silhouette edges; everything else is inference. Correct this file with scripts/trace_sprite_sheet.py rather than trusting it. Every joint absent from a frame's confidence map is estimated. _l is the near pair and _r the far pair, matching run-pose-trace-v1.json. Near/far leg ownership is not readable from this artwork at all: both legs share one palette and the shading encodes a light direction, not depth. Ownership below is assigned by kinematic continuity across the cycle, anchored on the two flight frames, and is the single thing most worth a human correcting. The cannon arm is treated as the near arm throughout because it is drawn over the torso; unlike the legs it does not change sides at the half cycle. Support labels come from which foot reaches the lowest occupied row; reference_04 and reference_09 reach only row 64 while the rest reach 65 to 66, so both read as flight.",
